local mainnotes                                           ///
    "Entries are proportional-odds ratios from ordered logit models; city-clustered standard errors are in parentheses." ///
    "Within each outcome, M1 and M2 use exactly the same complete expectation sample. M1 contains sex, age terms, education, equivalized household income, employment-school position, hukou/residence, city tier, region, CCP membership, and marital status. M2 adds household-income and job-stability expectations." ///
    "The sample comprises respondents aged 16-65 who answered the 2025 AI module, with no more than one respondent retained per household. Both ordered outcomes include confirmed nonusers as category zero." ///
    "Models use the configured 2025 `ai_analysis_weight' survey weight." ///
    "The Generative-versus-Specialised p-value comes from a joint ordered-logit gsem on the common two-outcome sample and tests equality of all common slopes; it does not by itself establish which association is stronger." ///
    "For job-stability expectations, non-employed respondents skipped by the questionnaire form a not-employed/not-applicable category. Genuine item nonresponse remains missing." ///
    "Reference categories are male, compulsory education or less, employed and not in school, not a CCP member, first-tier/new first-tier city, East region, and no expected change. Odds ratios above one indicate a higher position on the ordered outcome." ///
    "Proportional-odds diagnostics are written to the log when the installed diagnostic command accepts the weight and variance specification."

local linkednotes                                         ///
    "Entries are proportional-odds ratios from ordered logit models; city-clustered standard errors are in parentheses." ///
    "Within each outcome, L1-L4 use exactly the same people who answered the AI module in both 2023 and 2025. L1 contains 2023 structural position; L2 adds 2023 phone/computer resources; L3 adds AI awareness; L4 adds AI familiarity and prior use." ///
    "Models use the configured 2025 `ai_analysis_weight' survey weight and retain no more than one respondent per household." ///
    "Respondents routed out of the 2023 familiarity and use questions because they were unaware of AI are coded zero. Genuine missing follow-up responses among aware respondents remain missing." ///
    "Familiarity is standardized among aware respondents and set to zero for unaware respondents, so its L4 coefficient represents the familiarity gradient among those already aware of AI." ///
    "Device prices are IHS-transformed in thousand yuan; nonowners receive zero, while missing prices among owners are median-imputed with unreported missing-price indicators included." ///
    "The dependent variables are ordered incorporation measures: nonuse, one/two-to-five/more-than-five tools for breadth, and nonuse/up to 0.5/0.5-1/more-than-1 hour for daily time." ///
    "Reference categories are male, compulsory education or less, not employed, not a CCP member, first-tier/new first-tier city, and East region. Odds ratios above one indicate a higher position on the ordered outcome." ///
    "Proportional-odds diagnostics are written to the log when the installed diagnostic command accepts the weight and variance specification."

